Z||000000||fiero_hunter85||08-31-2001||08:59 AM||||does anyone know if late 80's to early 90's grand am wheels will fit on a fiero?<P><BR>i found a nice set of 16 inch wheels for only $200 and they are already painted white wich is the same color as the 85 GT i am getting.||||reg||5
Z||000001||OcalaFiero||08-31-2001||09:01 AM||||I'm almost positive that they fit, I know that the mid 80's grand am wheels fit, but have a slightly different offset.<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero_hunter85||08-31-2001||09:18 AM||||thanx for the help. now all i have to do is figure out what size tires i want. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||OcalaFiero||08-31-2001||09:26 AM||||If i remember correctly, on my '84 that I had about 5 years ago, I used 14inch grand am wheels (the hi-tech ones that looked like the Fiero wheels) with 205 or 215 /60 R14's. They looked great, didn't really affect the speedo and had no clearance problems in the front or back.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||08-31-2001||09:33 AM||||for tire size, use this calculator:<P><A HREF="http://www.miata.net/garage/tirecalc.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.miata.net/garage/tirecalc.html</A> it will also show you how far off your speedometer will be if you change tire size too much!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||08-31-2001||11:32 AM||||Yes, I'm using them with 225/50-16's. They are 47mm offset, but with the 225 width, the scrub radius is slightly smaller and they work like a dream. <P>They are 16x6J-47mm.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||08-31-2001||01:44 PM||||up through 98 will fit.  In '99 they went with the 5x115mm bolt pattern, so no 99+ Grand Am wheels will fit.||||reg||1
Z||000007||MinnGreenGT||08-31-2001||02:25 PM||||Was it '99 that they changed from the "Straight Honeycomb" style to the newer "Twisted Honeycomb" style?  I've always liked the look of the newer "twisted" wheels, but just assumed that they won't fit- at least not easily. Anyone know which wheels I'm talking about?<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||08-31-2001||07:02 PM||||No, we were hoping *you* knew which wheels you were talking about. <P>I'm talking about the late 80 and early 90's three vent wheels.||||reg||12
